  "configuration_id": "config_023",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_042) is the current best at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1 (3.60 GPU hrs). The RNA encoder is the largest performance lever (scgpt→0.507 vs scvi_n200→0.725, a 22-pt gap), but PCA_n2000 has never been tested in any multimodal setting. Question: Can the linear PCA_n2000 encoder approach scvi_n200's performance in the best-known architecture (transformer aggregation + weighted fusion + ViT-L image encoder)? Why this experiment: With 4 experiments remaining, reducing uncertainty about the RNA encoder is the highest-value move. If PCA matches scvi_n200, it confirms a cheaper, simpler alternative and frees remaining budget for fine-tuning other axes; if it falls well short, we confirm scvi_n200 is essential and can dedicate remaining runs to small refinements (e.g., single-profile variants or fusion tweaks) around the proven scvi_n200 stack. Expected relative cost: ~3–3.5 GPU hrs, slightly cheaper than config_042 since PCA replaces a trained neural encoder with a linear projection, while the ViT-L image branch and transformer aggregation dominate compute."
}

